o writeCoordArray() / writeParquet(<DuckDBArray>) should let the producer choose
  the within-partition row ordering (a cluster_by argument), the way the flat
  writers already do via zorder() / hilbert() / lexicographic cluster specs in
  DuckDBDataFrame (R/parquet-io-cluster.R). Today the DuckDB COO path
  hard-orders by rev(indexcols) (R/writeCoordArray-duckdb.R), the arrow path by
  nzwhich order, so a producer cannot ship, e.g., a COO clustered on the sample
  axis (or the feature axis). This is a FAITHFUL reorder: COO is order-agnostic
  on read, so no datapackage.json descriptor change and no scibis reader change;
  only regenerate any byte-exact goldens.
  - Lower cluster_by through the existing .clusterOrderSQL into the COO COPY
    builder's order_cols.
  - Motivation: benchmarking on a large spatial atlas showed that clustering the
    COO on the sample axis is a pure ordering change that makes a sample-range
    nnz count several-fold faster. The win is release-eligible and faithful;
    only the ordering knob is missing.

o Row-group size on the COO writer is already 491520 (240 x the 2048
  STANDARD_VECTOR_SIZE) on both the DuckDB path (R/writeCoordArray-duckdb.R) and
  the arrow path (R/writeCoordArray.R), from the benchmark in this package. Keep
  this as the shared convention; DuckDBDataFrame's lazy export path does NOT yet
  match it (see DuckDBDataFrame/TODO).
